AdaptiveCpp 25.10: include what you use in the runtime.

The Xcode 26 toolchain's libc++ removes transitive includes even under
-std=c++17, exposing every runtime file that uses std::vector/atomic/
memory/... without including the header (measured: rt-backend-omp fails
with "no template named 'atomic' in namespace 'std'" and friends;
libstdc++ provided these transitively on linux). Mechanically generated:
for each runtime-core/omp/generic file using a std symbol whose header it
does not include, the include is appended after the file's last existing
include. GPU-backend subdirectories are untouched (not built on macOS;
transitively fine with libstdc++ on linux). Upstream develop has the same
gaps; an include-hygiene PR there is the durable fix.

